h|broth]]\n* ½ cup prepared [[Cookbook:Salsa|salsa]]\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoons]] [[Cookbook:Garam Masala|garam masala]]\n* 1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] frozen [[Cookbook:Apple|apple]] juice concentrate\n* ¼ cup packed [[Cookbook:Cilantro|cilantro leaves]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# [[Cookbook:Purée|Purée]] all ingredients in a blender until smooth.\n# Heat in a large [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]] or [[Cookbook:Dutch Oven|Dutch oven]], and bring to a [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]].\n# Simmer, stirring often, 4–5 minutes, to blend flavors.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Garnish with ¼ cup plain [[Cookbook:Yogurt|yogurt]] and ¼ cup thinly [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]] [[Cookbook:Green onion|green onions]].\n* Replace the chicken broth with vegetable stock for a vegan dish.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chickpea]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground ginger]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garam masala]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken broth and stock]]\n[[Category:Recipes using apple juice]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Spicy Chickpea Soup","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cans (32 ounces) chickpeas, drained","sourceText":"2 cans (32 ounces) chickpeas, drained","amountText":"2 cans (32 ounces) chickpeas, drained","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 can (14 ounces) light coconut milk","sourceText":"1 can (14 ounces) light coconut milk","amountText":"1 can (14 ounces) light coconut milk","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1 cup low-sodium chicken broth","sourceText":"1 cup low-sodium chicken broth","amountText":"1 cup low-sodium chicken broth","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"